    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive strategy for July 29 hinges on capitalizing on favorable platoon alignments against mid-tier starting pitching. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.05) emerge as our premier starters, as both benefit significantly from positive park factors and favorable matchups against Yesavage and Sandoval, respectively. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is particularly well-positioned with a +14% dynamic platoon boost, solidifying his role as the anchor of the lineup. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (59.68) and **Jackson Merrill** (59.43) provide high-floor stability; while their scores are just below the \"Strong\" threshold, their high base projections against Emerson Hancock and Gabriel Hughes make them essential for maintaining counting-stat production.\n\nManaging the roster\u2019s peripheral risks requires close attention to the weather and high-end opposition. We are monitoring a 45% rain risk for **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, which could truncate their production if games are delayed. Furthermore, **Gunnar Henderson** faces a difficult assignment against the elite Skubal (2.62 xERA); his score reflects a significant -19% penalty for the opposing skill, forcing him into a lower-tier efficiency slot today. Among our bench options, **Dominic Smith** (45.19) came closest to cracking the starting nine, but he was ultimately relegated due to the combination of the aforementioned rain risk and a marginal efficiency rating against Christian Scott that failed to eclipse the starters currently holding utility and outfield spots.\n\nWe continue to prioritize speed and contact in this lineup, keeping an eye on **Andy Pages**, who holds an intriguing secondary advantage: the slow delivery of Hancock should provide a favorable environment for **Andy Pages** to potentially exploit the base paths, a critical edge for our categorical focus on stolen bases. As we await final lineup confirmations for **Jacob Wilson**, **Andy Pages**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Kyle Tucker**, these projections remain subject to minor volatility. We are proceeding with the assumption that these players hold their projected batting order positions, which currently provides the optimized path toward maximizing our 5x5 output.",
